WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.627
These are the key habits from Module 10.

00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:07.547
State the grain first. Use conditional aggregation for pivots.

00:00:07.547 --> 00:00:11.427
Use UNION ALL or lateral VALUES for unpivoting.

00:00:11.427 --> 00:00:14.922
Protect the distinction between NULL and zero.

00:00:14.922 --> 00:00:17.477
Validate totals and row counts.

00:00:17.477 --> 00:00:24.432
And choose long or wide form based on the downstream task, not because one format is always better.

00:00:24.432 --> 00:00:30.392
Connect this idea to a survey project reshaping question responses for analysis.

00:00:30.392 --> 00:00:36.152
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:36.152 --> 00:00:43.957
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:43.957 --> 00:00:49.602
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.602 --> 00:00:55.623
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
